  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_csb3",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1890,
        "y": -60
      },
      "text": "ECUMASTER CSB3 HARNESS - the CSB3 plug (HD36-24-33SE) and its switch inputs: cruise stalk, clutch and brake switches, the cruise ladder pull-up, and ONE 8-channel optocoupler board inline at the plug (Dan's on-hand board, 2026-10-13, C10-C13): brake (S9, +12V-active) -> input 01 -> output 01 -> S7 and reverse (B1, +12V-active) -> input 02 -> output 02 -> S8, both ground-active inputs (R56). Input COM to ground; the board's own 4.7k input resistors set the LED current. Output VCC from the CSB3 +5V (c3), never 12V: the board's 10k pull-ups go to VCC and the CSB3 S inputs are 'switched to ground' with no 12V rating (CSB3 manual v2.1 pp.3-5). Output GND to SGND (c4). Channels 03-08 not connected. Its +12V, ground and +5V wires come in broken off from ST185-A-cabin; the reverse switch output from ST185-B-cabin, the oil LED sink from ST185-ClusterLED and CAN H/L from ST185-CAN all arrive broken off with a note. Non-ECU harness."
    },
    {
      "id": "n_cavity_notes",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1890,
        "y": 630
      },
      "text": "CAVITY NOTES - full text of the signals marked * on this drawing\nECUMaster CSB3 - Power/CAN/Swi c26: L4 low-side - oil pressure LED sink (CAN 0x643); the wire from this pin to the LED is drawn on ST185-ClusterLED (broken off)"
    }
  ],
